              {
                "detail": "always is false and the skill does not request persistent platform-wide privileges. It reads local profile dirs and creates temporary files but does not modify other skills or agent configuration.",
                "label": "Persistence & Privilege",
                "name": "persistence_privilege",
                "rating": "ok"
              }
            ],
            "guidance": "This skill automates a real Chrome browser to post to Weibo and intentionally reuses your local Chrome profile (so you must be logged in). Before installing, consider:\n- It will read your Chrome user-data directories and interact with the active browser session (cookies/sessions) — only install if you trust the code and want it to act as your logged-in browser.\n- The scripts call host utilities (osascript/swift on macOS, xdotool/ydotool on Linux, wl-copy/xclip for clipboard, powershell on Windows) but the registry metadata only lists bun/npx; ensure you have the expected tools and understand the skill will fail or behave differently if they’re missing.\n- Because it sends real paste keystrokes and can activate applications, test it first with a disposable Chrome profile or in an environment without sensitive accounts open.\n- If you’re not comfortable with a skill reading DevToolsActivePort and scanning default Chrome profile paths, or running local native commands, don’t enable it or review the included source files yourself (they are bundled) to confirm there are no unexpected network endpoints or telemetry.\nIf you want higher assurance, run the scripts in a controlled environment, or ask the skill author for an explicit, minimal list of required host tools and a justification for accessing each Chrome profile path.",
